    "title": "bip158: include duplicate filter elements only once",
    "user": {
      "login": "Bruce039",
      "id": 109469941,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBoZg9Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109469941?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Bruce039",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The Contents section says what goes into a basic filter, but nothing in the BIP says that an item appearing more than once is only included once. Set Construction describes `L` as \"a vector of N raw items\", so building the filter from the text alone keeps duplicates.\n\nThat gives a different result from the test vectors. Block 926485 in `bip-0158/testnet-19.json` (\"Duplicate pushdata 913bcc2b...\") spends several outputs with the same script. Keeping every item gives N=17 and a filter and filter header that don't match. Removing duplicates gives N=9, which matches the vector. All other vectors come out the same either way.\n\nBitcoin Core (`GCSFilter::ElementSet` is a `std::unordered_set`) and btcd (`gcs/builder` collects into a map) both dedupe, so this only writes down what implementations already do.\n",
